Third-party data

The files under internal/catalog/data (the embedded settings catalogs) are
derived from the source code of Creality Print
(https://github.com/CrealityOfficial/CrealityPrint), which is licensed under
the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0.

What is taken from it is facts about the settings: their keys, value types,
ranges, choices, short labels, where the application shows them, and the
conditions under which a setting is enabled or forced by another. The catalog
contains no descriptive text written by Creality: the long descriptions the
tools show are read at run time from the message catalogs of the user's own
Creality Print installation and are never copied into this program or its
repository. The tool that generates the catalogs is tools/catalog-gen.

